      {
        "id": "ip_note",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          -40,
          340
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "## One panel, many filters\n\n**Filters** is an *Input Panel*: each line of its **Fields** setting is a field, and a field with a column filters **Sales** on it:\n\n```\nRegion = choice region style=buttons\nCity = choice city\nPrice = between price step=5\nOrdered = date range ordered\nIn stock = toggle in_stock\n```\n\n- **Cascade** \u2014 City only offers the picked Region's cities, and Price spans their prices.\n- **Apply** \u2014 the panel's *Apply changes* is *with an Apply button*, so set every field, then press **Apply filters**: one run. **Reset filters** puts them back.\n- **Same picks, second table** \u2014 the panel's **filters** output feeds **Same filters on orders**, which maps `region` to the orders table's `sales_region`.\n- **A control as a variable** \u2014 **Min quantity** publishes `${min_qty}`, and **Big orders** filters with `qty >= ${min_qty}`. No wire.\n",
          "width": 560,
          "height": 0
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null,
        "description": "",
        "active": true,
        "locked": false,
        "frozen": false,
        "manual": false,
        "frozen_fingerprint": null,
        "exclusive": null,
        "preview": true,
        "port_labels": null,
